The '''2008 FA Community Shield''' (also known as '''The FA Community Shield sponsored by [[McDonald's]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 86th staging of the [[FA Community Shield]], an annual [[association football|football]] match played between the reigning [[Premier League]] champions and [[FA Cup]] winners. The match was played on 10 August 2008 between [[2007–08 Premier League]] champions [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] and [[2007–08 FA Cup]] winners [[Portsmouth F.C.|Portsmouth]] as the "curtain-raiser" to the [[2008–09 in English football|2008–09 English football season]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.thefa.com/TheFACup/TheFACommunityShield/ |archive-url=https://archive.today/20060326121547/http://www.thefa.com/TheFACup/TheFACommunityShield/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=26 March 2006 |title=The FA Community Shield sponsored by McDonald's |access-date=6 March 2009 |date=27 February 2009 |work=TheFA.com |publisher=The Football Association }}</ref> The match marked the 100th year since the [[1908 FA Charity Shield|first Charity Shield]], also won by Manchester United after a replay in August 1908.

Manchester United won the game 3–1 on penalties, after the match finished 0–0 after 90 minutes; the Community Shield no longer plays extra time if the teams are level at the end of normal time.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/7549022.stm |title =Man Utd 0-0 Portsmouth (Man Utd win 3-1 on penalties)|date=10 August 2008|work=BBC Sport|access-date=7 August 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/manchester-united/2535218/Community-Shield-Manchester-United-reatin-Community-Shield-beating-Portsmouth-on-penalties-Football.html|title =Manchester United retain Community Shield beating Portsmouth on penalties|date=10 August 2008|work=The Daily Telegraph|access-date=7 August 2019}}</ref>	
	
The match was the second meeting between the two teams in the space of two weeks, after they had played each other in a friendly in [[Nigeria]] on 27 July 2008. It was also the first Community Shield since 1996 to feature a team from outside the big four of Manchester United, [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]], [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] and [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]]. With this Community Shield title, United extended their record number of wins in the competition to 13 (17 including shared titles). 

